er field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, `unsafeNoChangedPath` counts the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n115: | `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input, after `trustedCheckout` confirms each line's checkout is the project root or a marked arena. |\n116: | `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, bec